From: mscharged-port
Subject: Competitive play: a tournament set's player at home drafts first
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

The draft's first team picks first, and the draft sorts its teams by the
players' RANKED records: in a Recharged tournament set the same player
drafted first in every game, while the home side went in turn (0079).
The draft host now names the machine whose team goes first, the one of
the player at home in this game (a new field of the draft message,
mFirstMachine), and every machine puts that team first after the sort.
The game start then finds the sides already right (no swap). Outside a
set's game the field says -1 and the draft keeps its order.

